# Bifrost Forge World Engine Project Context

Bifrost Forge World Engine (or simply "the Engine") is a fully qualified BPMN 2.0 Workflow Engine built with Elixir/OTP, Ash Framework, Phoenix, and PostgreSQL 18+. It is one OTP application (`:bfw_engine`) whose subsystems are compile-time boundaries (the `boundary` library) with a strict dependency direction: Core never depends on Peripheral, Plugins, or API. Peripheral never depends on API. Plugins (`BfwEngine.Plugins`) depend on Core and on `BfwEngine.Api`.

## Key Invariants

- **`BfwEngine.Api`** (Ash Code Interface) is the single shared service layer — every wire adapter and every plugin converges here.
- **Core domains** (`BfwEngine.Types`, `BfwEngine.Execution`, `BfwEngine.Events`, `BfwEngine.Timers`, `BfwEngine.Expressions`, `BfwEngine.BPMN`, `BfwEngine.DMN`) and the plugin contracts (`BfwEngine.Plugin`, `BfwEngine.EngineFacade`) never import from API, Peripheral, or Plugins domains. `mix compile` rejects a call across an undeclared boundary edge.
- **Plugins** are in-BEAM OTP apps. They call `BfwEngine.Api.*` directly — no HTTP round-trip.
- **EngineEventBus** is the only channel through which observability, audit logging, and external integrations see engine events.

## Subsystem Layout

Each boundary lives under `lib/bfw_engine/<subsystem>/` (web: `lib/bfw_engine_web/`); unit tests under `test/unit/<subsystem>/` (test layout: `docs/architecture/testing.md` §Test layout). Dependency table and layer model: `docs/Architecture.md` §1 and §Subsystem Boundaries.

| Boundary | Domain | Purpose |
|-----|--------|---------|
| `BfwEngine.Types` | Core | Behaviour-free structs, shared types |
| `BfwEngine.Execution` | Core | PI/FNI runtime, resume, payload cap |
| `BfwEngine.Events` | Core | EngineEventBus, pending sweeper |
| `BfwEngine.Timers` | Core | ISO 8601 scheduler |
| `BfwEngine.Expressions` | Core | FEEL evaluator |
| `BfwEngine.BPMN` | Core | XML parser, ModelCache, linter gate |
| `BfwEngine.DMN` | Core | DMN parser and evaluator |
| `BfwEngine.Plugin`, `BfwEngine.EngineFacade` | Plugin contracts | Plugin behaviours, facade handed to plugins |
| `BfwEngine.Persistence` | Peripheral | Ash + AshPostgres, Mix `bfw.retention.purge` |
| `BfwEngine.Telemetry` | Peripheral | :telemetry counters, /stats |
| `BfwEngine.Plugins` | Plugins | Plugin registry, in-BEAM loader |
| `BfwEngine.Auth` | API | JWT validation |
| `BfwEngine.Api` | API | `BfwEngine.Api` service-layer facade |
| `BfwEngineWeb` | API | REST + GraphQL + WebSocket + Admin |

